<section class="content-section faq site-frame" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="section-rail"><p class="eyebrow section-inner">// FAQ</p></div>
  <div class="section-inner section-content faq-layout">
    <h2 id="faq-title">Frequently Asked<br />Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>Can I make an invoice without an account?</summary><p>
          Yes. Create and edit invoices in your browser without signing in. Your drafts stay
          on that device.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where are my invoices saved?</summary><p>
          Guest invoices are saved in this browser. Clearing site data removes them, so
          export JSON backups. Signed-in workspace records are saved to your account.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I download a PDF?</summary><p>
          Choose Export PDF in the creator, then Save as PDF in your browser's print dialog.
          The account workspace can also issue a locked invoice with its original archived
          PDF.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which currencies are supported?</summary><p>
          AED, EUR, USD, GBP, INR, CAD, AUD, and JPY. Tax labels, identifiers, and payment
          details are editable.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I host Shardlane myself?</summary><p>
          Yes. The source is available under MPL-2.0. The browser creator runs without
          service credentials; cloud records need the documented authentication, database,
          and storage configuration.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does Shardlane collect payments?</summary><p>
          No. Shardlane creates and manages invoice documents. It does not collect payments,
          send emails, or process recurring billing.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
